Material adapted, by letibot file:

  crates/ui/src/highlight.rs
      Adapted from crates/codegen/xai-grok-markdown/src/open_code_highlighter.rs
      — the resumable-lexer-state mechanism for highlighting a code fence that
      is still streaming: persist the state after the last newline-terminated
      line, keep the already-painted lines, repaint only the incomplete tail.
      Their measurements of the pre-fix quadratic behaviour are quoted in the
      module header.
      CHANGED: their state is syntect's ParseState + HighlightState and a theme
      file; letibot's is a hand-written line lexer whose state is two Copy
      fields. Their second strategy — a (fence_info, body) memo capped at
      256 KiB, needed because pulldown-cmark cannot checkpoint inside a list —
      is not ported, because letibot's markdown lexer hands a code body to the
      highlighter directly and the case does not arise. Language table, token
      classes and palette are letibot's.

  crates/ui/src/diff.rs
      Adapted from crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager-diff/src/lib.rs and
      crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/src/scrollback/blocks/tool/edit.rs — the
      hunk model, MAX_CONTEXT = 3, overlapping-hunk stitching, the
      unified-only rendering decision, and the empty-to-empty edge case
      ("must not produce a fabricated one-line insertion").
      CHANGED: they use the `similar` crate; letibot has a hand-written Myers
      with a `max_d` cap and an explicit `degraded` flag, because a letibot head
      is single-threaded over the same loop that services its socket. Word-level
      intra-line highlighting is added — grok-build has none. Their progressive
      per-hunk-then-whole-file syntax highlighting (EditHighlightPhase) is not
      ported; it requires a worker thread.

  crates/ui/src/card.rs
      Adapted from crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/src/scrollback/ — the
      three-state DisplayMode { Collapsed, Truncated, Expanded } (types.rs:52);
      the running/finished verb tense flip (blocks/tool/mod.rs:107); the head/
      tail truncation budgets 5/3, 10/3 and 2/3 (blocks/tool/read.rs:16,
      use_tool.rs:15, appearance/config.rs:613); the "… +N lines" elided marker
      as a separator row (blocks/tool/execute.rs:549); and from blocks/
      thinking.rs the "Thinking…" → "Thought for 4.2s" header, the ┃ rail, the
      decision to de-emphasise a reasoning body by *attribute* rather than by
      colour, and the rule that a replayed session must not render a fabricated
      "Thought for 0.0s".
      CHANGED: grok-build's block renderers are 750-3,000 lines each and are
      coupled to BlockContext / Theme / Selectable / AppearanceConfig; letibot's
      is plain data and one function. The inline/full byte-count disclosure and
      the abstention outcome are letibot's and have no grok-build counterpart.

  crates/tools/src/builtins/edit.rs
      Design read, no code taken:
      crates/codegen/xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/search_replace/
      — exact `match_indices` matching with the one relaxation off by default;
      `build_nearest_match_hint` (the longest whitespace-delimited token of the
      search string's first line, reported with a line number) is the shape of
      letibot's `anchor_lines`, re-implemented from the behaviour rather than
      copied; and the discipline of stripping a description sentence when the
      behaviour it describes is switched off, so the model is never told a rule
      that is not running. Their `search_replace/mod.rs:803` comment — that
      read-before-edit is *"encouraged via description and RL grading, not
      runtime-enforced"* — is quoted as the gap `crates/tools/src/files.rs`
      closes.

  crates/ui/src/progress.rs
      Adapted from crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/src/views/progress_bar.rs —
      eighth-of-a-cell bar resolution using the LEFT BLOCK glyphs, and the
      whole-cells-plus-remainder split.
      CHANGED: their bar is two-valued; letibot's is three-valued
      (cache-reused / computed-now / remaining), so the sub-cell remainder is
      applied only to the moving edge. The spinner is driven by elapsed
      milliseconds rather than by a frame tick, since a letibot head has no
      fixed frame rate.

  crates/ui/src/editor.rs
      Adapted from crates/codegen/xai-ratatui-textarea/src/editor.rs — the
      plan/apply split, WordStyle { Small, WhitespaceDelimited }, the undo
      batching rule (a cursor jump or a whitespace/non-whitespace transition
      breaks the batch), the rule that undo does not restore the kill buffer,
      and the sticky preferred column for vertical motion.
      CHANGED: rewritten against a plain String buffer with no ratatui, no
      selection model, no mouse and no elements; snapshots carry text and cursor
      only.

